  "body": "Ticket tracking discussion of restoring the [`URL.domainToASCII` and `URL.domainToUnicode`](https://github.com/whatwg/url/issues/63) functions or implementing something new.\r\n\r\n### Summary\r\nProcessing international domain name labels is tricky, slow, and requires large lookup tables.  However, browsers already perform this task (typically using the [ICU library](https://ssl.icu-project.org/download/4.4.html)) and could expose these functions to JavaScript.\r\n\r\nThe proposal to add this functionality was nixed because no major browser had implemented it. [Node supports the call](https://github.com/nodejs/node/blob/master/src/node_url.cc#L100) (<50 lines) and a WebKit developer chimed in saying it would be trivial to add.\r\n\r\nOne issue is **which** version of ToUnicode function should be exposed and whether there are other utility functions that might be needed, such as subdomain comparisons, distinguishing between domains/subdomains/TLD/public suffix, and IP address parsing.",
